# THANKS

C9Core is built upon the outstanding work of the AzerothCore project and
its long lineage of predecessors. Without their years of effort, C9Core
would not exist.

## AzerothCore
- **Project**: AzerothCore — open-source WoW 3.3.5a (Wrath of the Lich King) server emulator
- **Website**: https://www.azerothcore.org/
- **Source**: https://github.com/azerothcore/azerothcore-wotlk
- **License**: GNU GPL v2

AzerothCore provides the complete game emulation layer: world simulation,
player logic, scripting system, database schema, and networking
infrastructure that C9Core extends with cluster, proxy, and node management
capabilities.

## Upstream lineage (from AzerothCore AUTHORS)
- **TrinityCore** — https://www.trinitycore.org/
- **MaNGOS** — http://www.mangosproject.org (2005–2008), http://getmangos.com (2008–2011)
- **WoW Daemon Team** (2004)

## C9Core additions
The following systems are original work developed on top of AzerothCore
and are not present in the upstream project:

- **proxyserver** — transparent WoW protocol proxy with per-node routing,
  auto-scale triggers, and cross-node player directory
- **nodemgr** — per-node daemon that manages worldserver lifecycle and
  reports health to the proxy over a PSK-authenticated TCP channel
- **clustermgr** — ncurses-based TUI for cluster monitoring and node
  deployment (SCP/SSH wizard)
- **shared/Cluster/PskCrypt** — AES-256-CTR + HMAC-SHA256 channel
  authentication used by all three cluster components
